<path-to-java-executable>

Full path to the Java executable used by Burp Suite.
Example:
C:\\Program Files\\Java\\jdk-21\\bin\\java.exe
/path/to/mcp-proxy.jar

Full path to the MCP Proxy JAR file downloaded from the Burp MCP extension.
Example:
C:\\Users\\subha\\OneDrive\\Documents\\mcp-proxy.jar
<Burp-MCP-Server-URL>

URL where the Burp MCP Server is running.
Default value:
http://127.0.0.1:9876/
Important: When specifying Windows file paths in the JSON configuration, use double backslashes (\\) instead of single backslashes (\). JSON treats the backslash as an escape character, so double backslashes are required for paths to be parsed correctly.

Example Configuration

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "burp": {
      "command": "C:\\Program Files\\Java\\jdk-21\\bin\\java.exe",
      "args": [
        "-jar",
        "C:\\Users\\subha\\OneDrive\\Documents\\mcp-proxy.jar",
        "--sse-url",
        "http://127.0.0.1:9876/"
      ]
    }
  }
}
After updating the configuration:

Save the file (Ctrl + S).
Restart Cursor AI.
